    description: "Follow-up from the INV-zogud mypy ramp. Two error categories share a\nroot pattern: a local/loop variable is bound to two DIFFERENT types in one\nfunction scope (mypy flags [no-redef] for annotated re-declarations,\n[assignment] for loop-var reuse). Unlike the 22 already-fixed sites (benign\nre-annotation of the SAME-typed variable — dropping the second annotation\nwas a zero-change cleanup), these need a deliberate RENAME to separate the\ntwo conceptually-distinct variables, because the occurrences carry genuinely\ndifferent types AND pre-existing assignment/index errors.\n\nConfirmed sites:\n- framework_patterns.py: `symbol` — loop var (Symbol, line 1504) vs a\n  nullable lookup (Symbol | None, ~1603). Also 2 pre-existing assignment\n  errors (1603/1607).\n- scala.py: `meta` — two dicts with different value types (~459 vs ~561).\n  Also pre-existing index/assignment errors (~563).\n- Deferred-but-benign (excluded from the no-redef PR only to dodge the\n  java.py smart-test slice limitation, see the sibling tooling item):\n  java.py `meta` at 1022 and 1101 (these ARE the safe drop-annotation fix;\n  just re-land them once java.py can be touched without the coverage\n  false-negative).\n- Assignment loop-var reuse (rename): catalog.py `reg`\n  (RegisteredLinker vs RegisteredAnalyzer, ~470), supply_chain.py `match`\n  (Match[str] vs Path, ~885), websocket.py `file_path` (str vs Path, ~790).\n\nEach rename must update ALL references within the block (regression risk —\ntests catch a miss). Low priority; part of the broader mypy basic-mode\ncleanup toward WI-rabum (flip CI blocking) / INV-zogud (strict)."  # e717
    fields: {}  # e717
